Training and model changes

The original DQN training setup used a much larger and more software-oriented configuration:

replay buffer size: 100000
learning starts: 5000
batch size: 128
target update interval: 2000
exploration fraction: 0.4
final epsilon: 0.02
neural network: [256, 256]

In the FPGA-friendly version, you simplified this significantly:

replay buffer size reduced to 10000
learning starts reduced to 1000
batch size reduced to 64
target update interval reduced to 1000
exploration fraction reduced to 0.30
final epsilon changed to 0.05
neural network reduced to a single hidden layer [32]

The reward function itself was kept essentially the same as the earlier successful version, because it gave the best balancing performance.
